## Expert Summary

**Farzana Hasan, diamond expert** | [About Farzana](/about-farzana/)

The savings with lab-grown diamonds are real. A 1.5ct D-VVS1 lab stone costs $1,950 — the natural equivalent costs $10,000–$12,000. That difference changes what you can afford.

Lab savings unlock better grades: D instead of G, VVS1 instead of VS2, platinum instead of 14k gold. The total ring stays within budget. The grade improves dramatically.

The tradeoff is resale value. Lab diamonds are not investments — if you plan to trade in later, the numbers don't work. If you plan to wear it, the grade-for-budget calculation is unambiguous.

My recommendation: [D-VVS1 1.5ct at $1,950](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29116588?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Ridged Solitaire at $1,224](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-ridged-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147412?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). $3,174 total — D-VVS1 certified — complete ring.

